  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1238 PM MST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nAfter the passage of the system, northwest flow aloft covers the \nstate on Tuesday. Light snow cover across areas in northern and \neastern NM may limit high temperatures on Tuesday, but currently \nlooking at 40s and 50s once again (between 5-15F below average \nacross most of the forecast area). Weak ridging builds into place on \nWednesday, allowing temperatures to rebound closer to normal. A \ntrough/closed low is forecast to graze the western/southwestern part \nof the state through the Thanksgiving holiday, but minimal impacts \nare expected from it (PoPs are currently lower than 10%).  After \nthat disturbance passes, northwest flow looks to dominate the \nweekend, likely providing breezy conditions to locations along and \njust east of the central mountain chain. At this time, the next \nchances for rain and snow look to arrive late weekend or early next \nweek. However, model run to run consistency has been somewhat poor, \nso there is low confidence on this.",
